WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.980
Feifei: Hello and welcome to The English

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.200
We Speak. You are Neil...

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.120
Neil: ... and hello, you are Feifei.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.560
Feifei: Neil, a question - if you looked into

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.840
my purse, what would you find?

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.480
Neil: Not much! Probably lots of small

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.820
coins that aren't worth much.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.900
Feifei: Well I'm not rich, Neil - but yes, you

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.540
would find small change. A collection

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.200
of coins with little value.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.860
Neil: OK - is this the phrase for this

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.080
programme?

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.580
Feifei: Not exactly. The phrase is 'small

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.540
change' but it's not about money.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.420
Something that is insignificant or trivial,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.260
meaning not important,

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.680
can also be described as 'small change'.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.320
Neil: Like getting a seat on the train

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.060
during the rush hour is 'small change' for

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:49.720
me.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.520
Feifei: And getting chocolate sprinkles on

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.500
top of my cappuccino is

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.800
'small change' for me.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.220
Neil: Really? That's 'big change' for me!

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.100
Let's hear some examples that are far

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.820
from being small change!

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.900
I've only got a cold so my health problems

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.460
are small change compared with your

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.660
broken leg.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.280
Eating out every night is small change to

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.320
Molly - she can afford it with the huge

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.460
salary she's on.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.200
Where I sit on the plane is small change

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.840
to me, as long as we arrive on time.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.480
Feifei: This is The English We Speak from

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.760
BBC Learning English and we're talking

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.200
about the phrase 'small change' which

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.530
describes something insignificant

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.969
or trivial, meaning not important.

00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:41.340
Neil: We can also describe someone as

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.140
being 'small change' - so they are not

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.420
important. Feifei, do you think I'm small

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.840
change in this programme?

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.700
Feifei: Of course not, Neil. You are very

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.960
important to this programme - and

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.860
besides, we couldn't afford the other

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:53.540
presenter!

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.960
Neil: Ha ha. Very funny. So now we've

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.820
explained 'small change' - can you

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.160
lend me some?

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.660
Feifei: You mean money? How much do

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.360
you want?

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.860
Neil: Ten pounds!

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.500
Feifei: Neil, that's NOT small change - and

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.420
your request is not 'small change' either.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.100
The answer is 'no'!

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.440
Neil: Well it was worth a try. See ya.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.480
Feifei: Bye.

